# FA3 FP8 (e4m3) Forward Path — Reference Analysis

All paths are under `/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/` unless noted.

---

## 1. Tile Shapes for FP8 hd128 (vs BF16)

Tile selection is centralized in `tile_size.h`, called from `flash_fwd_launch_template.h` with `sizeof(Element)` (1 for e4m3, 2 for bf16/fp16):

```41:46:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_launch_template.h
    static constexpr std::tuple<int, int, bool, bool> kBlockMN_RS_IntraWGOverlap = tile_size_fwd_sm90(kHeadDim, kHeadDimV, Is_causal, Is_local, sizeof(Element) /*element_size*/, V_colmajor, PagedKVNonTMA, Has_softcap, Use_one_mma_wg);
    ...
    static constexpr int kBlockM = Arch >= 90 ? std::get<0>(kBlockMN_RS_IntraWGOverlap) : ...
    static constexpr int kBlockN = Arch >= 90 ? std::get<1>(kBlockMN_RS_IntraWGOverlap) : ...
    static constexpr bool MmaPV_is_RS = std::get<2>(kBlockMN_RS_IntraWGOverlap);
    static constexpr bool IntraWGOverlap = std::get<3>(kBlockMN_RS_IntraWGOverlap);
```

### BF16 hd128 (element_size=2)

```40:45:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_size.h
        } else if (headdim <= 128) {
            if (use_one_mma_wg) {
                return {64, is_causal || is_local || paged_kv_non_TMA ? 128 : 176, true, true};
            } else {
                return {128, is_causal || is_local || paged_kv_non_TMA ? 128 : 160, true, true};
            }
```

**BF16 prefill (default): `128 × 128` (causal/local/paged) or `128 × 160` (non-causal).** Decode (`use_one_mma_wg`): `64 × 128/176`.

### FP8 hd128 (element_size=1)

Two compile-time branches controlled by `FLASHATTENTION_DISABLE_FP8_TWO_LEVEL_ACCUMULATION` (enabled by default in vLLM builds):

```62:89:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/tile_size.h
        } else {
            // Prefill tiles — two-level accumulation needs smaller tiles to reduce
            // register pressure from the separate fp32 accumulator (tOrO_accum).
#ifndef FLASHATTENTION_DISABLE_FP8_TWO_LEVEL_ACCUMULATION
            ...
            } else if (headdim <= 128) {
                return {128, 192, true, true};
            ...
#else
            ...
            } else if (headdim <= 128) {
                return {128, paged_kv_non_TMA ? 160 : (v_colmajor || (softcap && is_local) ? 192 : 224), true, true};
```

| Mode | FP8 hd128 | BF16 hd128 |
|------|-----------|------------|
| **Prefill** (two-level accum, default) | **128 × 192** | 128 × 128/160 |
| **Prefill** (two-level disabled) | 128 × 224 (or 160 paged) | same |
| **Decode** (`use_one_mma_wg`) | **64 × 96** | 64 × 128/176 |

Decode heuristic (`heuristics.h:10-14`): SM90, d=64/128, not local, `seqlen_q * (h/h_k) ≤ 64`.

**All FP8 tiles force `MmaPV_is_RS = true` and `IntraWGOverlap = true`** (3rd/4th tuple elements). FP8 also **requires RS for PV**:

```86:87:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    static_assert(!(!MmaPV_is_RS && Is_FP8), "MmaPV must be RS if FP8");
    static_assert(!(!MmaPV_is_RS && Transpose_V), "MmaPV must be RS if Transpose_V");
```

The canonical vLLM instantiation is `flash_fwd_hdim128_e4m3_packgqa_sm90.cu` → `run_mha_fwd_<90, float_e4m3_t, 128, 128, ...>`.

---

## 2. Smem Layout / Swizzle for FP8 Q/K/V

FP8 detection and layout type aliases:

```45:68:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    static constexpr bool Is_FP8 = cute::is_same_v<Element, cutlass::float_e4m3_t> || cute::is_same_v<Element, cutlass::float_e5m2_t>;;
    ...
    static constexpr bool Transpose_V = Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor;
    ...
    static constexpr cute::GMMA::Major MmaMajorV = !Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor ? GMMA::Major::MN : GMMA::Major::K;
    static constexpr cute::GMMA::Major TmaMajorV = !V_colmajor ? GMMA::Major::MN : GMMA::Major::K;
```

### Q and K — K-major SW128 via CUTLASS selector

```130:138:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    using SmemLayoutAtomQ = decltype(cutlass::gemm::collective::detail::ss_smem_selector<GMMA::Major::K, Element,
        decltype(cute::get<0>(TileShape_MNK{})), decltype(cute::get<2>(TileShape_MNK{}))>());
    ...
    using SmemLayoutAtomK = decltype(cutlass::gemm::collective::detail::ss_smem_selector<GMMA::Major::K, Element,
        decltype(cute::get<1>(TileShape_MNK{})), decltype(cute::get<2>(TileShape_MNK{}))>());
```

For hd128, `BLK_K0 = 128`, so `ss_smem_selector` picks **`GMMA::Layout_K_SW128_Atom<Element>`** (`sm90_common.inl:301-303`).

### How 128B swizzle differs for 1-byte vs 2-byte

CUTLASS defines a **fixed 128-byte swizzle atom in bits**, then `upcast`s by element width:

```84:104:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/csrc/cutlass/include/cute/atom/mma_traits_sm90_gmma.hpp
using Layout_K_SW128_Atom_Bits  = ComposedLayout<Swizzle<3,4,3>, smem_ptr_flag, Layout<Shape<_8,_1024>,Stride<_1024,_1>>>;
...
using Layout_K_SW128_Atom = decltype(upcast<sizeof_bits<Type>::value>(Layout_K_SW128_Atom_Bits{}));
```

Same `Swizzle<3,4,3>` (128B), but:
- **fp8 (8-bit):** atom ≈ `Shape<8, 128>` elements → **128 fp8 cols per 128B swizzle tile**
- **bf16 (16-bit):** atom ≈ `Shape<8, 64>` elements → **64 bf16 cols per 128B swizzle tile**

Physical 128B footprint is identical; logical element tiling doubles along K for 1-byte types.

Alignment requirements (`mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp:305-309`):
- Q/K/V smem: **≥ 128B** alignment
- Transpose path: `smem_vt`/`smem_v` may need **512B** for `as_position_independent_swizzle_tensor` (comment at lines 654-655)

### V — dual layouts (TMA staging vs MMA)

```140:152:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    using SmemLayoutAtomVt = decltype(cutlass::gemm::collective::detail::ss_smem_selector<TmaMajorV, Element,
                                      Int<kHeadDimV>, decltype(cute::get<2>(TileShape_MNK_PV{}))>());
    ...
    using SmemLayoutAtomVtMma = decltype(cutlass::gemm::collective::detail::ss_smem_selector<MmaMajorV, Element,
                                         Int<kHeadDimV>, decltype(cute::get<2>(TileShape_MNK_PV{}))>());
```

For default FP8 row-major V (`V_colmajor=false`):
- **`TmaMajorV = MN`** → `SmemLayoutVt` in `smem_vt` (pre-transpose staging)
- **`MmaMajorV = K`** → `SmemLayoutVtMma` in `smem_v` (WGMMA B operand)

With `kBlockN=192`, `kHeadDimV=128`: both pick SW128 atoms (192 and 128 divisible by SW128 K atom size for fp8).

---

## 3. V Transpose for FP8 PV Matmul

### Why transpose is needed

Row-major V in gmem is **N×D** (seqlen × headdim). FP8 PV WGMMA needs V as **K-major B operand** (`MmaMajorV = K`). FA3 sets:

```57:57:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    static constexpr bool Transpose_V = Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor;
```

If `V_colmajor=true` (gmem stride: dim is contiguous), **no transpose** — TMA loads directly K-major.

### What happens (producer warp group)

1. **TMA loads V into `smem_vt`** with transposed gmem view (`shape_V = (headdim_v, seqlen, heads, batch)`, `mVt_TMA` at lines 688-702).

2. **In-smem transpose** via LDSM.T + byte permute + STSM.N:

```183:212:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    // Use LDSM.T and STSM to transpose V in the case of FP8 and V being row-major.
    ...
    using S2RTiledCopyVt = decltype(make_tiled_copy(
        Copy_Atom<SM75_U16x8_LDSM_T, Element>{}, ...));
    using R2STiledCopyV = decltype(make_tiled_copy(
        Copy_Atom<SM90_U32x4_STSM_N, Element>{}, ...));
```

3. **`transpose_V` lambda** (lines 759-776): LDSM.T load → `__byte_perm(upper, lower, 0x6420/0x7531)` on uint2 pairs → STSM store into `smem_v`.

4. **Pipeline**: separate `pipeline_vt` (TMA in) and `pipeline_v` (post-transpose, consumed by MMA). `copy_Vt_to_V` (814-828) runs transpose then fences + NamedBarrier on `TransposeBarrier`.

5. **Dual smem buffers** when `Transpose_V`:

```354:362:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
    struct TensorStorageTransposeV : ... {
        cute::array_aligned<Element, ...> smem_v;      // K-major for WGMMA
        cute::array_aligned<Element, ...> smem_vt;     // MN-major staging
        ...
    };
```

6. **Column permutation tradeoff** (lines 204-206): STSM layout permutes V columns; FA3 **un-permutes O columns** in epilogue (see §6).

For bf16 row-major V: `MmaMajorV = MN`, no transpose, single `smem_v`.

---

## 4. P (Softmax) → FP8 Conversion & Register Layout

### Pipeline per KV tile

After QK WGMMA + mask + online softmax:

```1229:1235:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
            softmax.template online_softmax</*Is_first=*/true, /*Check_inf=*/true>(tSrS);
            if constexpr (Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor) { flash::permute_Cregs_fp8(tSrS); }
            Tensor tOrP_acc = make_tensor(tSrS.data(), flash::convert_layout_acc_Aregs<TiledMmaPV>(tSrS.layout()));
            Tensor tOrP = make_tensor_like<Element>(tOrP_acc);
            convert_type_out(tOrP_acc, tOrP);
            if constexpr (Is_FP8 && V_colmajor) { flash::permute_Aregs_fp8(tOrP); }
```

Subsequent tiles reuse same layout, writing in-place into `tOrP` (lines 1275-1277).

### FP8-specific softmax scaling (`Max_offset=8`)

```433:433:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h
                flash::Softmax<..., /*Max_offset=*/!Is_FP8 ? 0 : 8> softmax(softmax_scale_log2);
```

In `scale_apply_exp2` (`softmax.h:64-68`): subtracts 8.0 from scaled max before `exp2f`, so post-exp values land in **[0, 256]** instead of [0,1], using more of e4m3 dynamic range. `finalize` divides `row_sum` by `2^8` when `Max_offset != 0` (lines 147-149).

### Layout transforms (SM90 FP8)

**QK accumulator (f32):** `((2, 2, N/8), MMA_M, MMA_N)`

**After `convert_layout_acc_Aregs` for 1-byte A (`utils.h:146-155`):**
```146:155:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/utils.h
            auto l = logical_divide(get<0, 2>(acc_layout), Tile<Layout<Shape<_2, _2>>>{});  // (((2, 2), N / 32))
            // This combines the first two modes (<0, 0> and <0, 1>) into one mode.
            // Will require register shuffling later to be correct.
            return make_layout(make_layout(Layout<_4>{}, get<0, 0, 0>(l), get<0, 0, 1>(l)),
                               get<1>(acc_layout),
                               coalesce(make_layout(get<0, 1>(l), get<2>(acc_layout))));  // ((4, 2, 2), MMA_M, N / 32 * MMA_N)
```

**Downcast:** `convert_type_out` uses `NumericArrayConverter<To, From, FragmentSize>` with vectorized fragment size = max type-size ratio (`utils.h:192-203`).

**Register permutes to match WGMMA RS A-operand (k32 tiles):**

| Path | When | Function | Fragment shape |
|------|------|----------|----------------|
| Pre-downcast | `!V_colmajor` (default) | `permute_Cregs_fp8` | f32: `((2,2,N/8), MMA_M, MMA_N)` — swaps adjacent pairs in mode-2 |
| Post-downcast | `V_colmajor` | `permute_Aregs_fp8` | fp8: `((4,2,2), MMA_M, MMA_N)` — quad shuffle + `__byte_perm` |

`permute_Aregs_fp8` (`utils.h:523-551`): recasts to `uint2`, uses `__shfl_sync` within 4-thread quads with `upper_map = {0,3,1,2}`, then `__byte_perm` with lane-dependent selectors `0x5410/0x1054` (upper) and `0x7632/0x3276` (lower).

**PV consumption:** P is always RS for FP8 — passed directly as `tOrP` to WGMMA:

```1256:1256:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
                flash::gemm<...>(tiled_mma_pv, cute::conditional_return<MmaPV_is_RS>(tOrP, tOsP), tOrV(...), tOrO);
```

`TiledMmaPV` uses `GMMA::rs_op_selector<..., TileShape_MNK_PV, GMMA::Major::K, MmaMajorV>()` (lines 110-111) → maps to **`wgmma.mma_async...m64nNk32.f32.e4m3.e4m3`** with K-tile=32, A=RS fp8, B=SS fp8 from smem.

---

## 5. Descale Folding (q/k/v)

Descale pointers: per-batch × KV-head, shape `(batch, h_k)` (`flash_api.cpp:1179-1207`).

### q_descale × k_descale → QK softmax scale

**Normal path (no softcap):** folded into `softmax_scale_log2` before Softmax construction:

```425:433:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/flash_fwd_kernel_sm90.h
                float softmax_scale_log2 = params.mainloop.softmax_scale_log2;
                if constexpr (Is_FP8 && !Has_softcap) {
                    ...
                    float const q_descale = ...;
                    float const k_descale = ...;
                    softmax_scale_log2 *= q_descale * k_descale;
                }
                flash::Softmax<..., Max_offset=8> softmax(softmax_scale_log2);
```

Host pre-computes base scale as `softmax_scale * M_LOG2E` (`mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp:585`).

**Softcap + FP8:** q/k descale folded into `softcap_val` instead (applied before tanh in score path):

```1109:1112:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
        if constexpr (Has_softcap && Is_FP8) {
            float const q_descale = ...;
            float const k_descale = ...;
            softcap_val *= q_descale * k_descale;
        }
```

**Not applied inside WGMMA QK itself** — fp8 matmul uses raw fp8 Q/K; descale is purely a softmax/score scaling correction.

### v_descale → output normalization (not softmax P)

Applied at tile end via `softmax.finalize(v_descale)`:

```1329:1339:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp
            float const v_descale = !Is_FP8 || params.ptr_v_descale == nullptr ? 1.0f : ...;
            finalize_dispatch(scores_scale, v_descale);
            ...
            softmax.rescale_o(tOrO, scores_scale);
```

`finalize` (`softmax.h:137-153`):
```142:145:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/softmax.h
            float inv_sum = (sum == 0.f || sum != sum) ? 0.f : 1.f / sum;
            scores_scale(mi) = inv_sum * final_scale;  // final_scale = v_descale
```

So: **`O = (P @ V) / row_sum × v_descale`**. Equivalent to dequantizing V before matmul. **Not applied in epilogue** — epilogue only converts f32→bf16 output (`flash_fwd_launch_template.h:212`: `T_out = bfloat16_t` for FP8).

Reference test semantics (`test_util.py:369-376`): descale Q/K/V in float before reference matmul — matches kernel factoring.

---

## 6. P-Layout Permutation & Intra-Warpgroup Reshuffling

FA3 has **three distinct FP8 permute functions** in `utils.h`:

### A. `permute_Cregs_fp8` — pre-downcast, default row-major V

```557:571:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/utils.h
CUTLASS_DEVICE void permute_Cregs_fp8(Fragment &frag) {
    // frag has shape ((2, 2, N / 8), MMA_M, MMA_N), each element is 32 bits
    ...
            cutlass::swap(frag_64b(make_coord(_0{}, _1{}, 2 * i), mi), frag_64b(make_coord(_0{}, _0{}, 2 * i + 1), mi));
```

Called when `Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor` after every `online_softmax`.

### B. `permute_Aregs_fp8` — post-downcast, V_colmajor path

Called when `Is_FP8 && V_colmajor` — full byte-level WGMMA A-operand shuffle (§4).

### C. `permute_output_fp8` — undo V-transpose column permutation on O accumulator

```577:594:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/utils.h
CUTLASS_DEVICE void permute_output_fp8(Fragment &out) {
    // out has shape ((2, 2, N / 8), MMA_M, MMA_N), each element is 32 bits
    ...
                cutlass::swap(frag(make_coord(_1{}, j, 2 * i), mi), frag(make_coord(_0{}, j, 2 * i + 1), mi));
```

Called in mainloop after final `rescale_o` when `Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor` (lines 1340, 1443, 1535).

### D. `permute_output_fp8_Vcolmajor` — epilogue undo for split/non-split

Because V-transpose STSM permutes columns, epilogue applies a **second, more complex shuffle** on output:

```244:250:/home/yak/data-fast/agent/reference/libraries/vllm-flash-attention/hopper/epilogue_fwd.hpp
        static constexpr bool NeedFP8Permute = FP8PermuteCol && (sizeof(Element) == 2 || sizeof(Element) == 4);
        if constexpr (NeedFP8Permute && Split) { flash::permute_output_fp8_Vcolmajor(tOrO); }
        Tensor tOrO_out = make_tensor_like<Element>(tOrO);
        flash::convert_type_out(tOrO, tOrO_out);
        if constexpr (NeedFP8Permute && !Split) { flash::permute_output_fp8_Vcolmajor(tOrO_out); }
```

`FP8PermuteCol = Is_FP8 && !V_colmajor` (launch template line 36). Uses quad shuffles with `upper_map = {0,2,3,1}` (`utils.h:610-631`).

### Why two output permutes?

Comment at `mainloop_fwd_sm90_tma_gmma_ws.hpp:204-206`:
> "Instead we will permute the cols of V, and un-permute the cols of O in the epilogue."

- **`permute_output_fp8`** in mainloop: fixes MMA accumulator layout after PV GEMM
- **`permute_output_fp8_Vcolmajor`** in epilogue: fixes column ordering from V-transpose STSM before gmem write

### Intra-warpgroup context

- FP8 uses **RS mode for P** (registers), SS for V (smem) — no P smem write on hot path
- `IntraWGOverlap=true` for all FP8 tiles: QK on one step overlaps with PV on previous tile within same warpgroup
- Transpose uses **`NamedBarrier::TransposeBarrier`** for warpgroup sync after STSM (line 827)
- FP8 PV uses **two-level accumulation** in `flash::gemm` (`utils.h:238-327`): backup fp32 acc, clear, WGMMA into temp, add back — reduces fp8 K-loop drift

---

## Quick Reference Summary

| Topic | FP8 e4m3 (hd128 prefill) | BF16 hd128 prefill |
|-------|--------------------------|---------------------|
| Tile | **128×192** | 128×128/160 |
| MmaPV | **RS** (P in registers) | RS |
| Q/K smem | K-major SW128 (128 fp8 cols/atom) | K-major SW128 (64 bf16 cols/atom) |
| V (row-major) | TMA→`smem_vt` (MN) → LDSM/STSM → `smem_v` (K) | TMA→`smem_v` (MN), no transpose |
| P path | f32 softmax → `permute_Cregs_fp8` → layout reshape → f32→e4m3 → RS WGMMA | f16/bf16 SS or RS, no permute |
| q/k descale | × into `softmax_scale_log2` | N/A |
| v descale | × in `finalize()` → `rescale_o` | N/A |
| Output dtype | **bf16** | same as input |

